    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added optional owner `postcode` support with region-based validation, following the codebase's established \"small policy class + one call in the create flow\" pattern to keep structural impact low.\n\n**Files changed (6):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (`pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$`). This gives the generated DTO its field, makes it stored/returned (via the `Owner` `allOf` inheritance), and enforces the 4-digit shape as a Bean Validation \u2192 malformed postcodes get an automatic **400**. No code written.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `postcode` column field plus a trivial getter/setter (CC 1 each). MapStruct auto-maps it by name in both directions, so no mapper change was needed.\n\n3. **`OwnerPostcodePolicy.java`** (new) \u2014 A small, self-contained policy holding the city\u2192region and region\u2192range tables. `rejectInvalidPostcode` returns early when the postcode is absent or the city's region is unknown, and throws a `@ResponseStatus(BAD_REQUEST)` exception only when a present postcode falls outside its region's range.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 One line (plus import) invoking the policy in the create flow, alongside the existing policy calls.\n\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added the `postcode VARCHAR(4)` column (the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`; h2 self-updates, and per repo precedent only hsqldb is maintained by hand).\n\n6. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 Appended a trailing `NULL` to the 10 seed owner rows to match the new column count.\n\n**Key correctness fix during development:** `Map.of(...).get(null)` throws NPE, so the policy looks up the region first and returns early before touching the range map \u2014 this is what makes a city with no known region (the test's random cities) accept any 4-digit postcode.\n\nBackward compatibility holds: owners created without a postcode are still accepted (verified by `coreAcceptsOwnerWithoutPostcode`).",
